  "goodToKnow": "Die Braunkohle is lignite, brown coal, mined in huge open pits (Tagebau) in the Rhineland, Lusatia (Lausitz) and central Germany. It's the most CO₂-intensive fuel, and Germany plans to end coal power by 2038 at the latest, 2030 in the Rhineland. Villages have been demolished for mines; the 2023 clearance of Lützerath drew large protests. Hard coal is die Steinkohle. It has no plural."
